xpf (0.0.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial xpf Debian package (increment A of #1917, subsumes #1923).
    Ships xpfd, xpf-userspace-dp, cli, the day-0 config-drive loader,
    and the systemd units. Binaries install to a dpkg-static staging
    path; live symlinks are created on first install only. The
    in-place upgrade cut-over mechanism is a separate increment.
  * The version field above is a placeholder; `make deb` rewrites it
    from `git describe` before building.
  * Quarantine ambiguous fabric zones away from MAIN routing/session fallback,
    require adjudicated zone stamps for multi-RI redirects, and fail closed on
    unstamped RI-node fabric ingress unless explicit legacy compatibility is
    enabled; reject cross-context zones at strict config commit (#11061).
  * Keep transit forwarding closed when the armed bridge-family barrier
    leg is unsupported; reject malformed SSH authorized_keys entries at
    apply (#10725).
  * Install live-address host-input fences on #1960/#10297 fail-closed
    cold boots, preserving management addresses while blocking data addresses
    until a valid config can be applied (#10732).
  * Install a separate pre-networkd host-input barrier before addresses become
    reachable; admit only loopback/L3/DHCP-client traffic, defer FRR/HA
    ingress, and hand off after enforcement or no-enforcement teardown (#10751).
  * Revoke authoritative userspace persistent NAT leases on clear, refresh the
    display mirror, propagate the operation to the HA peer, and fence stale
    SHOW refreshes and synced-session re-creation. Carry bounded clear fences
    across retained-pool allocator reseeds and same-address pool renames, even
    when no live reservations remain; prune expired keys and convert active-shell
    markers to a finite 60-second horizon when the shell itself is not carried
    (#10784).
  * Register day-0 and Debian maintainer-script regression tests with
    `make selftest` and census both test locations (#10747).
  * Mark subscriber-overrun gaps in CLI flow and packet-drop, gRPC packet-drop,
    and SSE streams, and expose flow-trace drop totals (#10834).
  * Report unknown interface duplex and surface counter/address read failures
    and unmatched interface filters in extensive interface output (#10843).
  * Include responder node identity in chassis-forwarding RPC responses and
    flag divergence between peer response identity and heartbeat belief
    (#10841).
  * Restrict `monitor traffic` to configured interfaces, require an explicit
    host-interface override, and report the requested and resolved capture
    devices (#10845).
  * Show config-sync divergence alarms without active configuration and report
    remote flow-monitor state as unknown (#10846).
  * Label cluster VRRP rows as configured and include per-group detail in
    gRPC cluster status (#10844).
  * Resolve default upgrade rollback targets and version GC from persisted
    committed predecessor history, excluding failed cuts (#10851).
  * Drop NAT64 IPv6 fragments whose Fragment Header names an extension header,
    preserving translated reassembly geometry (#10860).
  * Quarantine super-user event planting received over unauthenticated
    session-sync; preserve it for verified peers (#10870).
  * Preserve scheduler clock-safety and bounded republish retry state across
    config replacement, and retry failed or skipped initial schedule publishes
    (#10873).
  * Send match-all XFRM SA dump requests with the iproute2 address-filter
    attribute, avoiding malformed netlink attribute warnings (#11225).
  * Bound IKE/ESP rekey lifetimes and clamp tolerant DPD timers (#10882).
  * Escape helper errors and recent exception text in monitor terminal output
    (#10904).
  * Refuse MAC-pinned PCI bindings when a known-absent permanent MAC prevents
    identity verification (#10905).
  * Carry the validated fabric zone stamp into parked-fragment retries so
    overlap checks use the encoded zone's routing domain (#10917).
  * Stamp POLICY_DENY records with their evaluating config generation and
    leave stale queued or replayed policy IDs unattributed (#10978).
  * Seed fragment-association sharding, scope admission quotas to
    session identity, and drop associations when their admitting
    session closes (#11058).
  * Return accurate consumed-input counts from sanitizing writers on emit
    errors, permitting retries without duplicating already-emitted lines
    (#10900).
  * Complete factory-reset image-seal cleanup for regenerable device identity,
    managed service state, logs, and DHCP leases; refuse erasure while DDNS or
    IPsec teardown authority remains unresolved (#10769).
  * Prevent peer-echoed idle persistent-NAT leases, defer imported-lease
    promotion until successful local flow completion, restore full lease
    metadata after strict mirror refusal, and keep rollback safe across
    concurrent synced joins. Clamp skewed peer lifetimes at decode boundaries
    and imported lifetimes to the local timeout/schema ceiling (#10789).
  * Update same-key MASTER VIP changes in place; normalize address spelling,
    fence GARP/NA follow-ups before withdrawal, retain unannounced survivors,
    and bound send-lock scope to one VIP at a time (#10780).
  * Bind multi-zone snapshot authorization to the selected peer connection;
    keep stale-auth reports from re-arming after capable-peer convergence,
    make deferral reports and clears attempt-fresh across peer epochs and
    capability changes, and clear superseded alarms only after current active
    config succeeds; preserve local convergence after peer-only push failures
    (#10782).
  * Throttle REST authentication failures per source and account, harden SSH
    password login, and hash configured API-auth secrets (#10825).
  * Scope API-auth identities by login class and UTC expiry, require HTTPS for
    credentials, and migrate persisted credentials to bcrypt verifiers (#10826).
  * Redact named API-key `secret` values in REST config output and diagnostics,
    and hash API credentials received via peer config sync before persistence
    (#10826).
  * Throttle Basic and API-key verification, migrate credentials across active,
    rollback, rescue, and exported configs, and purge affected snapshots only
    from the xpf-owned local archive (#10825).
  * Include named API keys in local and remote `show system services` counts
    (#10826).
  * Flush box-oriented host-inbound conntrack entries and guard denied TCP/UDP
    replies before established accepts; disable TCP loose pickup at boot/runtime
    (#10752/#10764).
  * Scope stale host-input guards by ingress zone with trusted-reinject
    fallback, reassert verified TCP loose pickup disablement, and harden
    packet proof with HIGH exempt-UDP residual (#10752/#10764).
  * Resolve routing-instance ownership by Linux device identity, reject
    alias/tunnel dual claims, and quarantine ambiguous memberships on tolerant
    loads with an apply alarm and alertable metric (#11060).
  * Scope rib-group return paths to peer prefixes and peer tables so unrelated
    VRF misses cannot fall through to main; warn when next-table/PBR targets
    may lack a return route (#11062/#11320).
  * Warn about and exclude static routes without a forwarding disposition, so
    they cannot shadow an installable less-specific route in the helper FIB
    (#11327).
  * Index local and shared tuple identities for delayed session-close checks,
    preserving scoped-incarnation teardown while avoiding slab and shared-map
    scans under the shared-session mutex (#11299).
  * Route oversized same-binding flow-cache hits through pending-forward so
    normal egress MTU, PTB, and TCP-segmentation handling is preserved (#11376).

 -- xpf maintainers <noreply@anthropic.com>  Mon, 16 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000
